      "message": "WDYT about using the negated condition trick suggested in the bug?  That should cover NaNs without introducing special handling:\n\n```\n             if (!(c_pos \u003e o_pos)) {\n                 c_rec \u003d next_rec\u003cColorRec\u003e(c_rec, c_end);\n             }\n             if (!(o_pos \u003e c_pos)) {\n                 o_rec \u003d next_rec\u003cOpacityRec\u003e(o_rec, o_end);\n             }\n```\n\nAnother option is to check and advance NaN values individually (e.g. there\u0027s no reason to advance the opacity rec if only the color rec is NaN):\n\n```\n             if (SkIsNaN(c_pos) || c_pos \u003c\u003d o_pos) {\n                 c_rec \u003d next_rec\u003cColorRec\u003e(c_rec, c_end);\n             }\n             if (SkIsNaN(o_pos) || o_pos \u003c\u003d c_pos) {\n                 o_rec \u003d next_rec\u003cOpacityRec\u003e(o_rec, o_end);\n             }\n```\n\nI think this last version makes most sense.",
